    "zh": "短讲结束后，你将有三分钟检查作答。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "check"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen014.png",
    "sha256": "5a7b0c2ff908ba6b1f6a7712ed83f4eacd54f74ff5796d876260b82292ca4c04",
    "k": 13,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "transition",
    "en": "Fields and Branches of Anthropology.",
    "zh": "人类学的领域与分支。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "anthropology"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen015.png",
    "sha256": "c1d5793cdbee865fe2d3d68efca4dba6d06e06e928ddc351f9966e1da5662c65",
    "k": 14,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Good morning, everyone.",
    "zh": "大家早上好。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "Good morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen016.png",
    "sha256": "782eb8cde567642269db905200557ede5fb8ccd5120e46da06d081a8a9a28d66",
    "k": 15,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "In today’s lecture, I’m going to talk about anthropology.",
    "zh": "今天的讲座，我将谈谈人类学。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "anthropology"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen017.png",
    "sha256": "60e80296a1d2364b0966b23a7512baa8bd715241c699d639b103c73e4d30090b",
    "k": 16,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "It sounds a complicated word, right?",
    "zh": "这个词听起来很复杂，对吧？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "complicated"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen018.png",
    "sha256": "057b97236335ef190d5522252b9661c9c0228821b31c49f8c4b7a09d025bf9f6",
    "k": 17,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "You may want to know the origin of the word, or anything about anthropology.",
    "zh": "你们可能想知道这个词的来源，或是其他与人类学有关的知识。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "origin",
      "anthropology"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen019.png",
    "sha256": "c4150b545b7f9ed9faa0846ce167c585ab88d992ed57b39c112b8b7e726c784b",
    "k": 18,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Actually, the Greek word for “man” is “anthropos”.",
    "zh": "实际上，希腊语中表示“人”的词是“anthropos”。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "Greek"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen020.png",
    "sha256": "c50a540fcf3f9e35db285cd9548fe70eb22e9939ac06648fe4deca4a12a57246",
    "k": 19,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And to tell you the truth, the word anthropology has been in the English language for centuries.",
    "zh": "说实话，anthropology这个词在英语中已经存在几个世纪了。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "to tell you the truth",
      "century"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen021.png",
    "sha256": "4ae0a809e30c5f1805ae1b4ed46a57932fca4ffc1b60034d604549cc1f21aabc",
    "k": 20,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "But just what does the word anthropology mean?",
    "zh": "但anthropology究竟是什么意思呢？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "anthropology"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen022.png",
    "sha256": "a959caf9a86a83cce44c3d932ea0578f41315edd6f83618af65ea5d2f6e1ae8f",
    "k": 21,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Literally, anthropology means “the study of man”.",
    "zh": "从字面上说，人类学就是“对人的研究”。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "literally"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen023.png",
    "sha256": "b977029003f2b7ea95a75d9c7ffe01dc87d7e774abb9c8609a4e269be7dad9ec",
    "k": 22,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "As Paul Bohannan, who is a renowned anthropologist, pointed out a number of years ago, ",
    "zh": "正如著名人类学家保罗·博汉南多年前指出的：",
    "vocabulary": [
      "renowned",
      "anthropologist"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen024.png",
    "sha256": "962fda4077a43d2fabf6c0d0cde83b1c2f0a148212babec681b957ac27f328bf",
    "k": 22,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "“Each science that deals with people has its own definitions of human.",
    "zh": "“每一门研究人的科学，对人都有自己的定义。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "deal with",
      "definition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen025.png",
    "sha256": "89f22281f7ccba0ef4a992e7b426ea8f9f6e0a795642b08904c0ecb14dd8a8c8",
    "k": 23,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "An economist,” he explains, “defines a human as a choice-making animal.",
    "zh": "他解释道：“经济学家把人定义为会做选择的动物。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "economist",
      "choice-making"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen026.png",
    "sha256": "75da6452342a84614fdc9bfa75b907e93ef1b8a2731eb772b641461b7837e867",
    "k": 24,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Philosophers define man as a rationalizing animal...”",
    "zh": "哲学家则把人定义为善于为行为寻找合理解释的动物……”",
    "vocabulary": [
      "philosopher",
      "rationalize"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen027.png",
    "sha256": "0fb1c2b0a2c6f0844b979d689bb126fc94121f48d243d5ec3a02fac6795095ed",
    "k": 25,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And then, how does anthropology define humans?",
    "zh": "那么，人类学又是如何定义人的呢？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "define",
      "human"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen028.png",
    "sha256": "94af783adc5a3ec49060a09075b04f4059faca582d536a4a0aa5802a48062fd8",
    "k": 26,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Well, anthropology attempts to be all-inclusive in the study of human behavior in all places and throughout time.",
    "zh": "人类学力求全面研究所有地方、各个时代的人类行为。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "all-inclusive",
      "human behavior",
      "throughout time"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen029.png",
    "sha256": "9cdd35cdfed507168abaf2c956b26f397c79de10f9814d565b32899d732571f0",
    "k": 27,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Anthropology specializes in the description of humanistic, scientific, biological, historical, psychological and social views of humans.",
    "zh": "人类学专门从人文、科学、生物、历史、心理和社会等角度描述人类。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "specialize in",
      "humanistic",
      "biological",
      "psychological"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen030.png",
    "sha256": "24a1e5882cc22877f9c8bc11bffe8fbe4652913efc87a557a09e795436e48e35",
    "k": 28,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "To paraphrase Barbara Miller’s statement in her textbook, Cultural Anthropology, ",
    "zh": "用芭芭拉·米勒在其教科书《文化人类学》中的话来说，",
    "vocabulary": [
      "paraphrase"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen031.png",
    "sha256": "c068c0309d0cb2d6028c40cc6d76c1a52a560d6fdc9605a6688d71ae5bbf80de",
    "k": 28,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "the popular impression of anthropology is based mainly on movies and television shows that depict anthropologists as adventurers and heroes.",
    "zh": "大众对人类学的印象主要来自电影和电视节目，这些作品把人类学家描绘成冒险家和英雄。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "depict",
      "adventurer"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen032.png",
    "sha256": "ea8dfafe4ad5c61d2a012112d4ca6f59c95a21e926643aa9457668a57cb28bec",
    "k": 29,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Well, some do have adventures and discover treasures in Egyptian tombs and elsewhere, ",
    "zh": "有些人确实会经历冒险，在埃及陵墓等地方发现珍宝；",
    "vocabulary": [
      "Egyptian tombs"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen033.png",
    "sha256": "700176176cb2030fa5b4730f8ed8bf0503982a8a2b47ac43550b4da24a8f02b8",
    "k": 29,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "but mostly, their work is less glamorous and involves rather repetitive and tedious activities.",
    "zh": "但大多数时候，他们的工作并没有那么光鲜，而是涉及相当重复、乏味的活动。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "glamorous",
      "repetitive",
      "tedious"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen034.png",
    "sha256": "754b334f2abb49489081a6c9117f06241e4b80713bda1be20083c8c6062002d5",
    "k": 30,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Today, I’m not going into anthropologists’ adventures.",
    "zh": "今天我不打算详谈人类学家的冒险经历。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "go into",
      "adventure"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen035.png",
    "sha256": "9227709a520c95d1493644f90cf843fad88c6ea0ea6e816fd895e60a98e54144",
    "k": 31,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "What I’m going to do is to explain to you all the fields and branches of anthropology.",
    "zh": "我要向大家介绍的是人类学的各个领域和分支。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "field",
      "branch"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen036.png",
    "sha256": "9ff330ee94f245be0a8861e5b553a19f06d032ec85fd8ff5571f92597fbff6df",
    "k": 32,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Let’s begin by stating once again that anthropology is the study of human behavior in all places and at all times.",
    "zh": "我们先再次明确一点：人类学研究所有地方、各个时代的人类行为。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "state",
      "human behavior"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen037.png",
    "sha256": "0ed533cf5facec390ba6c2e17403d89e98076b31ee259dcb031061013e35f25a",
    "k": 33,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Western civilization takes credit for the development of anthropology, which, as a matter of fact, was a relatively late science.",
    "zh": "人类学的发展被归功于西方文明；事实上，它是一门出现得相对较晚的科学。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "Western civilization",
      "take credit for",
      "relatively"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen038.png",
    "sha256": "3c3829d5750774933c6c20d840abdb515ffb50fcc86b468916af9474ec791389",
    "k": 34,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Earlier Greek and Roman philosophers were more interested in speculating about the ideal society rather than describing those known to them.",
    "zh": "早期的希腊和罗马哲学家，更热衷于思考理想社会，而不是描述他们所知的现实社会。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "speculate",
      "ideal society",
      "rather than"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen039.png",
    "sha256": "44390796246e9d589add36b68eef1ad0fd87b7d75cc50576385617ec5b29b979",
    "k": 35,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "After the onset of the Age of Exploration, which included the discovery of the Americas, as well as travel to other distant places, ",
    "zh": "地理大发现时代开始后，随着美洲被发现以及人们前往其他遥远的地方，",
    "vocabulary": [
      "onset",
      "Age of Exploration"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen040.png",
    "sha256": "848bd55bd7d29581f5c1891eb11641d215a445b3c05f38ad3bc092288428cbb4",
    "k": 35,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "the study of non-Western people began in earnest.",
    "zh": "对非西方民族的研究才真正展开。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "non-Western",
      "in earnest"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen041.png",
    "sha256": "cf29451cdf38cbdd40938eb02759ad109d410249aa3b1f7ce13de6fbef31178e",
    "k": 36,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "In modern day, anthropology is a recognized social science with two broad fields and several branches or subfields.",
    "zh": "如今，人类学是一门公认的社会科学，包含两大领域和若干分支或次级领域。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "recognized",
      "social science",
      "subfield"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen042.png",
    "sha256": "98d06e5d5d6b8b18cc1f1cc9980bd5f9deffbde8e2d032326efb6aea7dc7a28f",
    "k": 37,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "OK. First, what are the two broad fields?",
    "zh": "好的。首先，这两大领域是什么？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "broad fields"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen043.png",
    "sha256": "18d17bf1f083d13adbee9d982de961e7dc187882b59961653833c2dd773c6f45",
    "k": 38,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "They are physical anthropology and cultural anthropology.",
    "zh": "它们是体质人类学和文化人类学。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "physical anthropology",
      "cultural anthropology"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen044.png",
    "sha256": "a4dbc387a147e470a48d5facf353c629563e76f2da71a73cf4cfa0136ae74d6b",
    "k": 39,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Let me give you a brief description of each.",
    "zh": "让我分别作个简要介绍。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "brief description"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen045.png",
    "sha256": "ccc9e03399713e6c73fa10b3c69229590a7b53ac66b0efdc8b08cfa90f610792",
    "k": 40,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Physical anthropology is concerned with the development of man as a mammal.",
    "zh": "体质人类学研究人类作为哺乳动物的发展过程。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "be concerned with",
      "mammal"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen046.png",
    "sha256": "8d64757b7b7718ff631ed395d2eb0895c26b0dafcd166a44d835844adea5a75e",
    "k": 41,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Related subjects are anatomy, biology and paleontology.",
    "zh": "相关学科有解剖学、生物学和古生物学。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "anatomy",
      "biology",
      "paleontology"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen047.png",
    "sha256": "81109dbbe5b44a075ebb1e22e9fcf71e332b2f182a300e4847e677542c9d987f",
    "k": 42,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Physical anthropologists study the evolution of the human species.",
    "zh": "体质人类学家研究人类这个物种的演化。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "evolution",
      "species"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen048.png",
    "sha256": "7b97bd727da461ce819559cb6ab9b78b90b19b14fbfeb7bdaecd040aff8c1421",
    "k": 43,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "One way they do this is by examining the fossils of what were once living creatures and living primates.",
    "zh": "其中一种研究方法，是考察过去生物留下的化石，以及现存的灵长类动物。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "fossil",
      "primate"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen049.png",
    "sha256": "afb2c72cde07bdde1ce4f140bf533954f42c7504765a4dd129d0c32277a21f9f",
    "k": 44,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Those include human beings.",
    "zh": "其中也包括人类。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "human beings"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen050.png",
    "sha256": "79def2f28865da8b6c53c36bb8f79ef6b96c29e544cad73b0457701db28cc629",
    "k": 45,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Common fossils are shells, bones and molds and imprints.",
    "zh": "常见的化石包括贝壳、骨骼，以及外模和印痕。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "shell",
      "mold",
      "imprint"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen051.png",
    "sha256": "4991c896fef002c317746dee8081c4c3e57b10c3067cbfe9342fea1d0aa46ebb",
    "k": 46,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "These are found buried in the earth or permanently frozen in glaciers.",
    "zh": "这些化石有的埋藏在地下，有的永久冻结在冰川中。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "bury",
      "permanently",
      "glacier"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen052.png",
    "sha256": "fb7d0ab40ee253d36fa5b95992652411559e2b800b28b3fedd3e789319278610",
    "k": 47,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Living primates are analyzed in order to study the mechanics of evolution and genetic differences among human populations.",
    "zh": "研究人员通过分析现存的灵长类动物，研究演化机制以及不同人群之间的遗传差异。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "mechanics",
      "genetic differences",
      "population"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen053.png",
    "sha256": "fe2f987cdbb3e34cff093b96fc9c9819a5c67399c49dcf2bd134e2adac4de510",
    "k": 48,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "OK, next, let’s talk about cultural anthropology.",
    "zh": "好，接下来我们谈谈文化人类学。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "cultural anthropology"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen054.png",
    "sha256": "e7f3c47806550256ef17d8e72662f7031598a34e3491ed5332d86480334bbc4a",
    "k": 49,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "This field is the study of learned behavior in human societies.",
    "zh": "这一领域研究人类社会中后天习得的行为。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "learned behavior"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen055.png",
    "sha256": "3c0fc8a713ac1b2df4de1a8a34ffcb938035c6cd393e679398d3913b2734fbd3",
    "k": 50,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 3,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Most cultural anthropologists would limit themselves to a few geographic areas, ",
    "zh": "大多数文化人类学家把研究范围限定在几个地区，",
    "vocabulary": [
      "limit oneself to",
      "geographic areas"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen056.png",
    "sha256": "dc23fd978d34702a5c34d0d9861ee22a3bd868c8b65805688bba932c659f75b6",
    "k": 50,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 3,
    "role": null,
    "en": "for example, Margaret Mead in Samoa and New Guinea, ",
    "zh": "例如研究萨摩亚和新几内亚的玛格丽特·米德，",
    "vocabulary": [
      "New Guinea"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen057.png",
    "sha256": "e94e85fcdc08898e7cdc7fe962be98764250d105b40c3a822b8fdb3742aeb5dc",
    "k": 50,
    "part": 3,
    "parts": 3,
    "role": null,
    "en": "and Clyde Kluckhohn with the Navajo Indians in the Southwestern United States.",
    "zh": "以及研究美国西南部纳瓦霍印第安人的克莱德·克拉克洪。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "southwestern"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen058.png",
    "sha256": "e46775adf9a2cab4f1748bd03973d93ebc37c22304a04543b77d6e4851261de5",
    "k": 51,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "I should mention that Kluckhohn’s work, which is Mirror for Man, is considered one of the best introductions to anthropology.",
    "zh": "我还要提一下，克拉克洪的著作《Mirror for Man》被认为是最出色的人类学入门读物之一。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "Mirror for Man",
      "introduction"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen059.png",
    "sha256": "2e8c15e35c69c8ce8e613dfeeb2d96ceb07ee01eaa6cfb04299d1dfaa0b5c74b",
    "k": 52,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Cultural anthropology and the scientific study of human culture will be discussed in more detail in our next lecture.",
    "zh": "下次讲座，我们将更详细地讨论文化人类学以及对人类文化的科学研究。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "scientific",
      "in more detail"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen060.png",
    "sha256": "5e7a3d693b682c8e27521634793c5b772102918cc1e978efd2ddfa95104f9003",
    "k": 53,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Today, we just take a brief look at the subfields of cultural anthropology.",
    "zh": "今天，我们只是简要了解一下文化人类学的各个分支。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "take a brief look at",
      "subfield"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen061.png",
    "sha256": "35634fc4281d8bd0d1c3b9bfd41eae682a5e7d1dfb95ddd308702593970ef8e7",
    "k": 54,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "They are archaeology, linguistics and ethnography.",
    "zh": "它们是考古学、语言学和民族志。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "archaeology",
      "linguistics",
      "ethnography"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen062.png",
    "sha256": "223dc6b743a25ddcfe545739b7818657ab55a8708a1bdf0a43e1fc2551777546",
    "k": 55,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So, what is archaeology?",
    "zh": "那么，什么是考古学？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "archaeology"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen063.png",
    "sha256": "421d9aefdf758fcbeb9e9792ee6925ead536c936e3140b1da154ecd41eec3f39",
    "k": 56,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "It is the study of different cultures through material sources, through historical objects that still remain today, ",
    "zh": "考古学通过物质资料，也就是留存至今的历史器物，研究不同文化，",
    "vocabulary": [
      "material sources",
      "historical objects"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen064.png",
    "sha256": "64dabfb09abdd020731f45ea6a921549279ee0fbb4793342dc12047a5dcb6ad5",
    "k": 56,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "rather than direct interviews or observations of the group under study.",
    "zh": "而不是直接访谈或观察所研究的群体。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "under study"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen065.png",
    "sha256": "b5cf82e0a4de1c09c48f68a0b7f26b876ca06b173d446958e21e3a0ebfeec1aa",
    "k": 57,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "One famous example of archaeological study is King Tut’s Tomb near Luxor, Egypt, which was discovered in 1922.",
    "zh": "考古研究的一个著名例子，是1922年在埃及卢克索附近发现的图坦卡蒙陵墓。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "archaeological",
      "tomb"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen066.png",
    "sha256": "e50dc8e33420f61955d354aa62a791294f64ccf614203b8d1be9be1dadb029b4",
    "k": 58,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Another subfield of cultural anthropology is linguistics, as I said just now.",
    "zh": "正如我刚才所说，文化人类学的另一个分支是语言学。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "linguistics"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen067.png",
    "sha256": "25737e7cd0547947e0863a41971bc0b00bc31f7ae5a83b83b7ac110e5b1da825",
    "k": 59,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "As you probably know, linguistics is the study of language as communication among humans.",
    "zh": "大家可能知道，语言学研究作为人类交流工具的语言。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "communication"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen068.png",
    "sha256": "351803a0dab9f4e4dafce5f6e66e3bd5a2ba6b40bf96befdf30d6f5445b8a246",
    "k": 60,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Culture is learned and transmitted primarily through language.",
    "zh": "文化主要通过语言被习得和传承。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "transmit",
      "primarily"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen069.png",
    "sha256": "e250bb04198023799cfa601b3bb910f18901f7b21d37b87f9d3d886304ba2f1b",
    "k": 61,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 3,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And ethnography, a subfield of cultural anthropology, is on the whole the systematic description of human societies, ",
    "zh": "民族志是文化人类学的一个分支，总体上是对人类社会的系统描述；",
    "vocabulary": [
      "on the whole",
      "systematic"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen070.png",
    "sha256": "32a3cc7809504238bc088ef041cf6351c2b77e8e972942793d20c26b0fcfba74",
    "k": 61,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 3,
    "role": null,
    "en": "mostly based on gathering the firsthand information about something in a real natural environment, ",
    "zh": "它主要在真实的自然环境中收集关于某事物的第一手资料，",
    "vocabulary": [
      "firsthand information"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen071.png",
    "sha256": "0a7cb48e4e763d4bcb99c9539608eef68d1806c167d6235274709e82a81b7ca1",
    "k": 61,
    "part": 3,
    "parts": 3,
    "role": null,
    "en": "rather than in a place of study, such as a laboratory or classroom.",
    "zh": "而不是在实验室或教室等研究场所中进行。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "laboratory"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen072.png",
    "sha256": "547bfdd6e1076cbd848b647b0053a8256a4b293bf9810dfc268475e21b8b1c2d",
    "k": 62,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Based on ethnographies, anthropologists can provide explanations of the behavior of different peoples.",
    "zh": "人类学家可以依据民族志，解释不同民族的行为。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "ethnography",
      "people"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen073.png",
    "sha256": "57a9bdefe6ebfdd23d5554d308c23fe2e08352964642cb229f1bca85d16492d8",
    "k": 63,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Let me also mention very briefly psychological anthropology, which deals with human personality and feelings.",
    "zh": "我还想非常简要地提一下心理人类学，它研究人的个性和情感。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "psychological anthropology",
      "personality"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen074.png",
    "sha256": "341209951d9622bce6ea160b564b15b86e3b0be2c36ddd32972e3864cf68da39",
    "k": 64,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "These are greatly influenced by an individual’s biological and mental characteristics as well as physical surroundings and personal experiences.",
    "zh": "个性和情感很大程度上受到个体的生理与心理特征，以及周围物质环境和个人经历的影响。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "characteristic",
      "physical surroundings",
      "personal experiences"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen075.png",
    "sha256": "cd5584e9dd0e3ad3f643de1d6f567f2eb52695ee259341770e2c2ab8206ae67b",
    "k": 65,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Related subjects are psychology and psychiatry.",
    "zh": "相关学科有心理学和精神病学。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "psychology",
      "psychiatry"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen076.png",
    "sha256": "bac63133a816232d10fe3df77e72b46691cc6c2ba63d360d1e57f5c9fdbbb22b",
    "k": 66,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And it is important to note that there are several universal features common among all societies; ",
    "zh": "需要指出，所有社会都有一些普遍特征，",
    "vocabulary": [
      "universal features"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen077.png",
    "sha256": "e485af2097c761bcffdd87957699f0d7d090294a26d429b981c2e89dbeed0c17",
    "k": 66,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "for example, the basic similarities in human biology and the existence of two sexes.",
    "zh": "例如人类生物学上的基本相似性，以及两种性别的存在。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "similarity",
      "sex"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen078.png",
    "sha256": "48bb3c94a9deec307eaae591e18b1f54748ab64cf1b62bd26d9a0d04c537685d",
    "k": 67,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Another of these universal features is education — either formal or informal or both.",
    "zh": "教育也是这些普遍特征之一，可以是正式教育、非正式教育，或二者兼有。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "formal",
      "informal"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen079.png",
    "sha256": "de7259cf2102443bb5955b17a6019e234fc0082a6ede0a2357edbd1c2e638007",
    "k": 68,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Education is necessary to provide the young with the skills and attitudes needed to carry on as adults.",
    "zh": "教育必不可少，因为它使年轻人具备成年后生活所需的技能和态度。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "provide",
      "carry on"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen080.png",
    "sha256": "fa717bf1d1ac3bceb89087d6377fa61544bdafb86c0e69984d0933079887c4f4",
    "k": 69,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So, you might ask, what are the practical applications for such a broad field of anthropology?",
    "zh": "那么，你们可能会问：人类学涉及如此广泛的领域，究竟有哪些实际应用呢？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "practical applications"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen081.png",
    "sha256": "593ffd04286d9a48926dcc2161bf3ba8e6820a09f02c01c161d448766ead61c3",
    "k": 70,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "The answer is that anthropology helps us plan the future and helps us contribute to the solution of human problems.",
    "zh": "答案是，人类学帮助我们规划未来，并为解决人类问题作出贡献。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "contribute to",
      "solution"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen082.png",
    "sha256": "af2d12eca5a95233a1da327d43b83aa3dad2da2eb747701c75bb185bc173db9b",
    "k": 71,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "You know, the newest area of the study of man is applied anthropology.",
    "zh": "大家知道，研究人类的最新领域是应用人类学。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "applied anthropology"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen083.png",
    "sha256": "ab9de6002eb4a8668899cfc2b6f1219e9abad19a03062fcdd7a0ed4bd504ddec",
    "k": 72,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Formerly, anthropology was limited to the academic field, and most anthropologists were teachers or museum curators.",
    "zh": "过去，人类学仅限于学术领域，大多数人类学家是教师或博物馆馆长。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "formerly",
      "academic",
      "curator"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen084.png",
    "sha256": "159e6a3d89a3bf8e0b1ac36534fdeca5c0486dfac0684110389ff68b9e2aba39",
    "k": 73,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "But for the past several decades, large numbers of “anthro” graduates have been employed in other fields, ",
    "zh": "但在过去几十年中，大量人类学专业毕业生受雇于其他领域，",
    "vocabulary": [
      "decade",
      "graduate"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen085.png",
    "sha256": "06fa57b1dac48daf81733ed0cb90c7ee47844cab6eb366092cfc3bf4e34a43d5",
    "k": 73,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "such as urban planning and administration, health care and international development.",
    "zh": "例如城市规划与管理、医疗保健和国际发展。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "urban planning",
      "administration",
      "health care"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen086.png",
    "sha256": "62f0378eeb3969051d47834ba450cee697941efdb23551077e1ad65ecac24a88",
    "k": 74,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "This shows that anthropology is not just an academic discipline.",
    "zh": "这表明，人类学并不只是一门学术学科。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "academic discipline"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen087.png",
    "sha256": "45649fd432f7694a99d3e2ad1f1425817304b88cf0a8df6a4089a69e1637648f",
    "k": 75,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "It has social and practical applications.",
    "zh": "它也有社会层面和实际层面的应用。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "application"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen088.png",
    "sha256": "84ecc8b382398855ed02281770b130f25b2ae8de6583e1855b366e92f7001019",
    "k": 76,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "OK, to wrap up, we have briefly talked about the definition, development and the fields and branches of anthropology.",
    "zh": "好，总结一下：我们简要谈过了人类学的定义、发展、领域和分支。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "wrap up",
      "definition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen089.png",
    "sha256": "e2b580802192f0428a050d308b6278652204340ad9e1506deb1e573753b61668",
    "k": 77,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "I hope after today’s lecture, you will understand that anthropology is not a scholarly field only.",
    "zh": "希望听完今天的讲座，大家能明白人类学并非只是一个学术领域。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "scholarly"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen090.png",
    "sha256": "98be2325129e2f346467b10c86e8d33fa54dc9262301e88289bd17effa2ba196",
    "k": 78,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "What’s more important is that although anthropologists have taken up the task of recording the processes and changes of cultures past and present, ",
    "zh": "更重要的是，人类学家在承担记录过去和当下文化发展过程及变化这一任务的同时，",
